# /etc/shade-tree/uptime-probe.env — EnvironmentFile for shade-tree-uptime-probe.service (systemd) and the
# crontab line in monitoring/uptime/crontab.example. Nothing here is secret: a bootnode onion and
# a PUBLIC signer key. Fill in the NEW fleet's values from network/<name>/bootnode.json.
#
# EITHER name a CURRENT v4 network record (resolved by packages/node/lib/network-record.mjs; a `pending` or
# retired record makes the probe report misconfig, which is correct — there is nothing current
# to probe yet). Replace the value before enabling this line:
#SHADE_TREE_NETWORK=your-v4-network
# OR pin the discovery inputs explicitly (these override the record when both are set):
#SHADE_TREE_BOOTNODE_ONION=<v4-bootnode-56-char>.onion
#SHADE_TREE_DIR_SIGNER=<v4-directory-signer-64-hex, no 0x>
#
# The public Grove observer targets the current v4 research Grove with
# SHADE_TREE_PROBE_ACCEPT_PRE_V4_CAPS=0. Set it to 1 only for a deliberately isolated observer
# of a named legacy fleet; never enable legacy capability verification for a current v4 Grove.
#
# Optional:
#SHADE_TREE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
#SHADE_TREE_DIR_MAX_AGE_SEC=300
#SHADE_TREE_DIR_FUTURE_SEC=300
